69
00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:57.618
I was like, "You were so good in your documentary."

70
00:02:57.618 --> 00:02:59.520
Right. (laughs)
Which isn't how you-

71
00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.740
I don't know if, you're not acting in that.

72
00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:03.180
It's an odd compliment to give,

73
00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:05.300
but he was like, "Thanks, I remember you

74
00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.800
from when you were six years old in my game room."

75
00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:12.120
He was so nice, and he taught us all how to paint,

76
00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.930
he took us on hikes, he's the nicest person

77
00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.492
I think I've ever met in my entire life.

78
00:03:16.492 --> 00:03:19.993
He really is, and he is a Jack of all trades.

79
00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:21.743
Yes.
You never know

80
00:03:21.743 --> 00:03:22.580
